      "reason": "HOT ZONE. Written from `git show 05c22146ef -- packages/kernel/trust-kernel/src/index.ts` (+42/-1): `createTrustKernel` takes a new `config: TrustKernelConfig` carrying `trustAnchors`, a module-private `CONFIGURED_ANCHORS` WeakMap keyed by the handle holds them, and `configuredTrustAnchors` is a new export. That is a change to construction, not a read of it. The WeakMap keying is the load-bearing part: only a caller already holding the unforgeable handle can read the anchors, and a forged object reaches nothing because it was never a key. `createTrustKernel` still performs no I/O — the boot path reads configuration and passes the result — so the constructor stays total. An earlier version of this entry said P1-02 only READS `signatureRoots` and does not change construction, which was simply false."
